Error [jet.ImportedScriptExecutes]: Imported script `helper.jet` has executable top-level statements
  --> helper.jet:1:1
    |
  1 | print("dependency")
    | ^^^^^
 Why: Imported files provide declarations; executable code belongs in an explicit `run: fn`, so an import never gains a hidden side effect.
 Fix: Move the statements into the entry file's `run: fn`, or import a declaration-only file
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0620
